 Also called: Edge neighbor lookup, Face neighbor lookup
 ## Overview
-Neighbor Configuration Lookup Tables provide a constant-time, grid-aware method for determining the spatial relationship between adjacent tetrahedra in a structured tetrahedral grid. They solve the problem of analytic traversal and boundary detection by mapping local topological indices (face or edge) to global neighbor offsets and displacements, enabling efficient isosurface extraction and subdivision without geometric intersection tests [S1]. This method is distinct from sibling methods like [Projected Tetrahedra](877-projected-tetrahedra.md) which rely on rasterization, and [Marching Tetrahedrons Algorithm](940-marching-tetrahedrons-algorithm.md) which uses static lookup tables for scalar field signs; instead, it uses explicit neighbor connectivity data to navigate the mesh structure directly [S1].
